WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.800 --> 00:00:02.400
If you’re anything like me,

00:00:02.400 --> 00:00:06.560
you have lots of ambitious
plans for the future.

00:00:06.560 --> 00:00:09.160
I’ve got a whole series of
new books I want to write,

00:00:09.160 --> 00:00:11.400
thousands more
videos to script.

00:00:11.400 --> 00:00:13.360
But guess what?

00:00:13.360 --> 00:00:16.760
None of us may be able to do
any of the things we want to do

00:00:16.760 --> 00:00:20.240
if we don't have our health.

00:00:20.240 --> 00:00:22.480
Welcome to the
NutritionFacts Podcast.

00:00:22.480 --> 00:00:25.320
I’m your host,
Dr. Michael Greger.

00:00:25.320 --> 00:00:29.440
There are all kinds of claims about
the red wine compound resveratrol.

00:00:29.440 --> 00:00:34.040
One is that it helps us live longer
and it benefits our metabolic health.

00:00:34.040 --> 00:00:36.440
But what does the science say?

00:00:36.440 --> 00:00:37.560
In our first story, we ask:

00:00:37.560 --> 00:00:42.520
is the red wine molecule responsible
for the so-called “French paradox”?

00:00:42.520 --> 00:00:46.200
Resveratrol became a
household word in 1991

00:00:46.200 --> 00:00:49.320
when a scientist
from Bordeaux University

00:00:49.320 --> 00:00:51.440
appeared on the popular TV show
"60 Minutes"

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:54.480
and attributed
the so-called French Paradox

00:00:54.480 --> 00:00:57.800
to the French habit
of drinking red wine.

00:00:57.800 --> 00:00:59.640
The term "French Paradox"
itself

00:00:59.640 --> 00:01:01.440
was coined in the newsletter

00:01:01.440 --> 00:01:04.400
of the International
Organization of Vine and Wine

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.880
to explain a curious finding.

00:01:06.880 --> 00:01:08.520
If you chart death
from heart attack

00:01:08.520 --> 00:01:09.920
versus the amount
of saturated fat

00:01:09.920 --> 00:01:11.920
and cholesterol consumed
in different countries,

00:01:11.920 --> 00:01:13.720
there appears to be
a straight line.

00:01:13.720 --> 00:01:15.960
The more animal-based foods
populations eat,

00:01:15.960 --> 00:01:18.120
the higher their death rates
appear to be.

00:01:18.120 --> 00:01:20.120
However, two countries
didn't fall in line

00:01:20.120 --> 00:01:21.520
with that straight line.

00:01:21.520 --> 00:01:23.720
Finland seemed to be doing
worse than expected,

00:01:23.720 --> 00:01:27.000
and France appeared to be doing
better than expected.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:28.800
Hence, the paradox.

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:30.600
How could France
have saturated fat

00:01:30.600 --> 00:01:32.240
and cholesterol intake
similar to Finland,

00:01:32.240 --> 00:01:35.240
but five times fewer
fatal heart attacks?

00:01:35.240 --> 00:01:38.280
Everyone had their pet theories
to explain the paradox.

00:01:38.280 --> 00:01:39.520
Was it the wining?

00:01:39.520 --> 00:01:40.960
Was it the dining?

00:01:40.960 --> 00:01:42.520
Yes, animal foods
are associated

00:01:42.520 --> 00:01:44.160
with coronary heart disease
mortality,

00:01:44.160 --> 00:01:46.480
but plant foods
appear to be protective.

00:01:46.480 --> 00:01:48.000
So, might the fact
that the French were eating

00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:49.640
four times as many vegetables

00:01:49.640 --> 00:01:52.120
help account
for their lower death rates?

00:01:52.120 --> 00:01:53.480
It turns out, however,

00:01:53.480 --> 00:01:56.920
that there may be
no paradox at all.

00:01:56.920 --> 00:01:58.080
According to an investigation

00:01:58.080 --> 00:01:59.280
by the World Health
Organization,

00:01:59.280 --> 00:02:01.800
French physicians were
just under-reporting

00:02:01.800 --> 00:02:04.400
heart disease deaths
on the death certificates.

00:02:04.400 --> 00:02:06.480
So, if you correct for that,

00:02:06.480 --> 00:02:08.680
France basically comes
right back in line

00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:10.280
with the death
versus animal fat

00:02:10.280 --> 00:02:12.560
and death
versus cholesterol lines,

00:02:12.560 --> 00:02:14.360
with about four times
the fatal heart attack rates

00:02:14.360 --> 00:02:17.960
as Japan and about four times
the animal fat consumption.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:20.000
By the time of the correction,
however,

00:02:20.000 --> 00:02:22.440
resveratrol research
had already taken root,

00:02:22.440 --> 00:02:24.280
culminating in more than 17,000

00:02:24.280 --> 00:02:27.240
scientific publications to date.

00:02:27.240 --> 00:02:29.360
But only about 1 to 2 percent
of the published reports

00:02:29.360 --> 00:02:31.560
were human clinical trials,

00:02:31.560 --> 00:02:33.600
and after many millions
of dollars spent

00:02:33.600 --> 00:02:35.600
and many years
of disappointing results,

00:02:35.600 --> 00:02:38.480
the scientific tide
started to turn.

00:02:38.480 --> 00:02:41.600
Reviews began to ask whether
resveratrol was a molecule

00:02:41.600 --> 00:02:44.000
whose time had come and gone:

00:02:44.000 --> 00:02:46.000
"Should we now consign
resveratrol

00:02:46.000 --> 00:02:47.760
to our intellectual
garbage cans

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:49.840
and move on to better things?"

00:02:49.840 --> 00:02:51.200
Of course,
it didn't help matters

00:02:51.200 --> 00:02:53.200
when a leading
resveratrol researcher

00:02:53.200 --> 00:02:57.160
was found guilty of 145 counts
of fabrication

00:02:57.160 --> 00:02:59.120
and falsification of data,

00:02:59.120 --> 00:03:02.480
throwing the whole field
into turmoil.

00:03:02.480 --> 00:03:06.160
But in 2013, resveratrol
was primed to make a comeback

00:03:06.160 --> 00:03:09.240
with the apparent confirmation
that it was a STAC,

00:03:09.240 --> 00:03:12.040
a sirtuin-activating compound,

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:14.560
that is, a compound
that purportedly activates

00:03:14.560 --> 00:03:16.640
a longevity enzyme.

00:03:16.640 --> 00:03:19.320
This has been called
into question, though.

00:03:19.320 --> 00:03:23.520
Commentaries with titles like
"Is resveratrol an imposter?"

00:03:23.520 --> 00:03:26.080
"Promising therapeutic,
or hopeless illusion?"

00:03:26.080 --> 00:03:29.120
and "The resveratrol fiasco"
were published,

00:03:29.120 --> 00:03:31.720
suggesting that the seeming
sirtuin activity

00:03:31.720 --> 00:03:34.720
was probably the result
of experimental artifacts.

00:03:34.720 --> 00:03:38.840
"In summary," a recent review
concluded, "the jury is out."

00:03:38.840 --> 00:03:40.120
The proof is in the pudding,
though.

00:03:40.120 --> 00:03:43.280
Does resveratrol enhance
longevity or not?

00:03:43.280 --> 00:03:45.440
Yeast is the big success story,

00:03:45.440 --> 00:03:47.400
with resveratrol
extending the lifespan

00:03:47.400 --> 00:03:50.160
of brewer's yeast
by up to 70 percent.

00:03:50.160 --> 00:03:52.800
Resveratrol also helped
microscopic roundworms

00:03:52.800 --> 00:03:55.760
live longer,
but it failed fruit flies,

00:03:55.760 --> 00:03:59.880
mosquitoes, and water fleas.

00:03:59.880 --> 00:04:02.080
Anything bigger than
a unicellular fungus

00:04:02.080 --> 00:04:04.040
or a microscopic worm?

00:04:04.040 --> 00:04:07.440
Yes, resveratrol can extend
the lives of honeybees

00:04:07.440 --> 00:04:09.880
and, most excitingly,
two vertebrates,

00:04:09.880 --> 00:04:10.920
short-lived fish:

00:04:10.920 --> 00:04:14.400
Gunther's
and turquoise killifish.

00:04:14.400 --> 00:04:16.960
Unfortunately, most studies
on mammals (mostly mice)

00:04:16.960 --> 00:04:20.360
failed to show
a lifespan benefit.

00:04:20.360 --> 00:04:21.920
Resveratrol is said
to extend the life

00:04:21.920 --> 00:04:23.440
of so-called model organisms

00:04:23.440 --> 00:04:25.760
by mimicking
calorie restriction,

00:04:25.760 --> 00:04:27.240
but flies and mice show

00:04:27.240 --> 00:04:30.080
robust life-extension responses
to dietary restriction,

00:04:30.080 --> 00:04:32.960
yet don't seem responsive
to resveratrol.

00:04:32.960 --> 00:04:35.640
That may just be true
of healthy animals, though.

00:04:35.640 --> 00:04:38.760
Give resveratrol to mice
in extremis,

00:04:38.760 --> 00:04:40.840
whether bombarded by radiation,

00:04:40.840 --> 00:04:42.000
poisoned with endotoxins,

00:04:42.000 --> 00:04:44.000
or having their intestines
punctured

00:04:44.000 --> 00:04:45.880
to cause sepsis-induced
kidney failure,

00:04:45.880 --> 00:04:48.360
and they do survive longer
with resveratrol

00:04:48.360 --> 00:04:52.080
than they otherwise would
under those circumstances.

00:04:52.080 --> 00:04:54.000
Resveratrol
can also help mediate

00:04:54.000 --> 00:04:58.120
the life-shortening effects
of high-fat diets in mice.

00:04:58.120 --> 00:04:59.720
The lifespans
of healthy mice and rats

00:04:59.720 --> 00:05:02.680
fed normal diets are not
affected by resveratrol,

00:05:02.680 --> 00:05:04.360
but the compound
partially prevented

00:05:04.360 --> 00:05:08.320
the premature deaths of mice
fed high-fat diets.

00:05:08.320 --> 00:05:10.880
The authors of a meta-analysis
of the effect of resveratrol

00:05:10.880 --> 00:05:12.920
on longevity across species
concluded

00:05:12.920 --> 00:05:14.960
that, based on the fact
that most mouse studies

00:05:14.960 --> 00:05:16.440
failed to show a benefit,

00:05:16.440 --> 00:05:19.520
it's "inappropriate
for resveratrol to be marketed

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:22.480
as a life-extending
health supplement."

00:05:22.480 --> 00:05:24.480
True, no study has demonstrated

00:05:24.480 --> 00:05:27.760
resveratrol lifespan extension
in healthy rodents,

00:05:27.760 --> 00:05:31.720
only in "metabolically
compromised mammals,"

00:05:31.720 --> 00:05:34.040
but isn't that
a pretty accurate description

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:37.400
of most of the U.S. population
these days?

00:05:37.400 --> 00:05:39.960
Studies on monkeys fed diets
high in butterfat and sugar

00:05:39.960 --> 00:05:41.880
found that resveratrol
decreased

00:05:41.880 --> 00:05:44.640
artery and abdominal fat
inflammation.

00:05:44.640 --> 00:05:46.480
Combined with the shift
towards normalizing

00:05:46.480 --> 00:05:49.200
the lifespans of mice
on high-fat diets,

00:05:49.200 --> 00:05:50.640
pharmacology journal
commentaries

00:05:50.640 --> 00:05:51.720
were published with titles

00:05:51.720 --> 00:05:55.720
like "Resveratrolâ€”pills
to replace a healthy diet?"

00:05:55.720 --> 00:05:58.840
speculating whether
"resveratrol is the compound

00:05:58.840 --> 00:06:01.040
that will allow us to be
more and more inactive

00:06:01.040 --> 00:06:02.480
while eating too much
in general

00:06:02.480 --> 00:06:05.760
and too much fat and sugar
in particular."

00:06:05.760 --> 00:06:08.240
Yes, a nutrition journal
editorial entitled

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:11.200
"Dodging physical activity
and a healthy diet" conceded,

00:06:11.200 --> 00:06:12.840
exercise and dietary
modification

00:06:12.840 --> 00:06:15.920
are the "most potent, cheapest,
and easiest ways

00:06:15.920 --> 00:06:18.760
to prevent lifestyle-related
chronic diseases,"

00:06:18.760 --> 00:06:20.680
but might resveratrol
on its own

00:06:20.680 --> 00:06:22.680
"take the edge
off the consequences

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:24.560
of your lifestyle?"

00:06:24.560 --> 00:06:27.480
No wonder annual sales
of resveratrol supplements

00:06:27.480 --> 00:06:30.520
reached $30 million
in the U.S. alone.

00:06:30.520 --> 00:06:32.000
Approaching the peak
in interest

00:06:32.000 --> 00:06:35.080
around the time Oprah Winfrey
mentioned it in 2009,

00:06:35.080 --> 00:06:37.120
it was estimated
that two-thirds of people

00:06:37.120 --> 00:06:38.280
in the United States taking

00:06:38.280 --> 00:06:40.400
multiple daily
dietary supplement regimens

00:06:40.400 --> 00:06:42.320
included resveratrol.

00:06:42.320 --> 00:06:46.680
But what does
the human data show?

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:50.832
I'll cover that, next.

00:06:50.920 --> 00:06:52.880
To see if the amount
of resveratrol you get

00:06:52.880 --> 00:06:55.440
from drinking red wine
might be beneficial,

00:06:55.440 --> 00:06:58.200
researchers looked to
the Chianti region of Tuscany

00:06:58.200 --> 00:07:00.320
to determine whether the levels
achieved through diet

00:07:00.320 --> 00:07:02.760
help protect
against long-term frailty,

00:07:02.760 --> 00:07:05.200
inflammation,
cardiovascular disease,

00:07:05.200 --> 00:07:06.880
cancer, or death.

00:07:06.880 --> 00:07:08.680
And the answer?

00:07:08.680 --> 00:07:10.200
None of the above.

00:07:10.200 --> 00:07:12.400
The amount of resveratrol
flowing through their systems

00:07:12.400 --> 00:07:14.760
didn't correlate with any
of the health outcomes studied

00:07:14.760 --> 00:07:16.520
over nine years of follow-up.

00:07:16.520 --> 00:07:17.760
This is surprising

00:07:17.760 --> 00:07:20.000
even if only because of
the confounding factors

00:07:20.000 --> 00:07:22.240
associated
with wine consumption.

00:07:22.240 --> 00:07:24.640
Wine drinkers may be
less likely to smoke

00:07:24.640 --> 00:07:26.040
and tend to have higher IQ,

00:07:26.040 --> 00:07:27.680
higher parental
education levels,

00:07:27.680 --> 00:07:29.680
and higher
socioeconomic status,

00:07:29.680 --> 00:07:31.480
which would be expected
to correlate

00:07:31.480 --> 00:07:33.160
with better health outcomes.

00:07:33.160 --> 00:07:35.320
In contrast, beer drinkers
suffer the oppositeâ€”

00:07:35.320 --> 00:07:37.840
lower IQ, parental education,
and social class.

00:07:37.840 --> 00:07:41.120
The average IQ
of wine-drinking men is 113,

00:07:41.120 --> 00:07:45.080
compared to 95
among beer-drinking men.

00:07:45.080 --> 00:07:47.040
Yet still, there appeared
to be no correlation

00:07:47.040 --> 00:07:50.080
between resveratrol exposure
and well-being.

00:07:50.080 --> 00:07:52.240
This may be because
wine-drinking populations

00:07:52.240 --> 00:07:54.920
may only be averaging
less than a milligram

00:07:54.920 --> 00:07:57.400
of resveratrol a day.

00:07:57.400 --> 00:08:00.240
Some "experts" recommend
a daily dose

00:08:00.240 --> 00:08:02.280
of 1 gram of resveratrol,

00:08:02.280 --> 00:08:05.080
based on the dosing used
in laboratory animal studies.

00:08:05.080 --> 00:08:06.800
How much red wine
would you have to drink

00:08:06.800 --> 00:08:08.000
to get that much?

00:08:08.000 --> 00:08:11.080
Eight thousand glasses a day.

00:08:11.080 --> 00:08:12.320
Not a fan of red wine?

00:08:12.320 --> 00:08:13.760
A couple thousand gallons

00:08:13.760 --> 00:08:15.240
of white wine a day
would do it,

00:08:15.240 --> 00:08:18.320
or 5,000 pounds of apples
or grapes,

00:08:18.320 --> 00:08:20.320
50,000 pounds of peanuts,

00:08:20.320 --> 00:08:22.600
a couple thousand pounds
of chocolate,

00:08:22.600 --> 00:08:26.040
or nearly a million bottles
of beer on the wall.

00:08:26.040 --> 00:08:27.720
The natural levels
of resveratrol

00:08:27.720 --> 00:08:29.880
found in foods and beverages
is not considered

00:08:29.880 --> 00:08:32.280
to be sufficient
to elicit health effects,

00:08:32.280 --> 00:08:33.440
but that doesn't
necessarily mean

00:08:33.440 --> 00:08:35.600
supplements wouldn't work.

00:08:35.600 --> 00:08:38.800
However, the bioavailability
of even high-dose resveratrol

00:08:38.800 --> 00:08:40.760
has been called into question.

00:08:40.760 --> 00:08:43.280
Maximum blood levels after
resveratrol supplementation

00:08:43.280 --> 00:08:45.640
can be as low as 40 nanomolar,

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:47.520
which is more than
a hundred times lower

00:08:47.520 --> 00:08:51.880
than the 5,000 to 250,000
nanomoles used in vitro

00:08:51.880 --> 00:08:53.800
to demonstrate
resveratrol effects.

00:08:53.800 --> 00:08:56.400
Even a five-gram dose
of resveratrol

00:08:56.400 --> 00:08:59.560
may fall short
of the required level.

00:08:59.560 --> 00:09:00.960
This is in contrast to rodents,

00:09:00.960 --> 00:09:04.920
in which blood levels
of 32,000 have been reported.

00:09:04.920 --> 00:09:07.440
Resveratrol is rapidly absorbed
in humans

00:09:07.440 --> 00:09:10.520
but is rapidly metabolized
in our intestine and liver;

00:09:10.520 --> 00:09:13.960
so, very little
free resveratrol remains.

00:09:13.960 --> 00:09:17.320
But there are about 20
resveratrol-derived metabolites

00:09:17.320 --> 00:09:19.560
that can end up in circulation
at much higher levels,

00:09:19.560 --> 00:09:21.680
like 20,000 nanomolar,

00:09:21.680 --> 00:09:24.600
that might have biological
activity of their own.

00:09:24.600 --> 00:09:26.240
What about using
the turmeric trick

00:09:26.240 --> 00:09:27.800
of adding black pepper
to suppress

00:09:27.800 --> 00:09:31.200
our body's natural
detoxification mechanisms?

00:09:31.200 --> 00:09:33.080
It works in mice.

00:09:33.080 --> 00:09:35.920
The black pepper compound
piperine

00:09:35.920 --> 00:09:37.800
increases maximum
blood concentrations

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:41.200
of resveratrol
more than 1,000 percent,

00:09:41.200 --> 00:09:42.200
but, unfortunately, it failed

00:09:42.200 --> 00:09:45.840
to significantly alter
blood levels in people.

00:09:45.840 --> 00:09:48.320
In a 2014 medical journal
editorial entitled

00:09:48.320 --> 00:09:50.760
"The resveratrol fiasco,"

00:09:50.760 --> 00:09:54.640
the Editor-in-Chief summarized
the state of the science:

00:09:54.640 --> 00:09:56.600
"The conclusions
are quite clear-cut:

00:09:56.600 --> 00:09:59.440
after more than 20 years
of well-funded research,

00:09:59.440 --> 00:10:04.160
resveratrol has no proven
human activity."

00:10:04.160 --> 00:10:05.320
However,
since that publication,

00:10:05.320 --> 00:10:07.840
more than 150
human clinical trials

00:10:07.840 --> 00:10:09.040
have been published.

00:10:09.040 --> 00:10:10.760
What's the update?

00:10:10.760 --> 00:10:14.400
Resveratrol was initially
envisaged as an antioxidant,

00:10:14.400 --> 00:10:16.760
but meta-analyses
of randomized controlled trials

00:10:16.760 --> 00:10:19.640
of resveratrol supplements
failed to find

00:10:19.640 --> 00:10:22.000
clinically or even statistically
significant effects

00:10:22.000 --> 00:10:23.880
on systemic markers
of oxidative stress,

00:10:23.880 --> 00:10:27.960
helping to explain the lack
of apparent DNA protection.

00:10:27.960 --> 00:10:31.680
Maybe it only helps with
the metabolically compromised?

00:10:31.680 --> 00:10:33.600
As one resveratrol review asked,

00:10:33.600 --> 00:10:35.160
"What conclusions would we draw

00:10:35.160 --> 00:10:37.040
about the efficacy
of penicillin

00:10:37.040 --> 00:10:38.720
if it had been tested
only among persons

00:10:38.720 --> 00:10:41.400
in the pink of condition?"

00:10:41.400 --> 00:10:43.200
Resveratrol does not appear
to improve

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:45.218
the metabolic function
of nonobese,

00:10:45.218 --> 00:10:46.360
nondiabetic individuals,

00:10:46.360 --> 00:10:48.760
or even benefit
overweight nondiabetics,

00:10:48.760 --> 00:10:50.480
nor does it help people
lose weight,

00:10:50.480 --> 00:10:52.400
but resveratrol may help

00:10:52.400 --> 00:10:55.680
with blood sugar control
in diabetics.

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:57.320
For almost all outcomes

00:10:57.320 --> 00:10:58.920
measured in randomized
controlled trials

00:10:58.920 --> 00:11:00.760
of type 2 diabetes,
metabolic syndrome,

00:11:00.760 --> 00:11:02.640
or nonalcoholic
fatty liver disease,

00:11:02.640 --> 00:11:05.240
the effects of resveratrol
were trivial,

00:11:05.240 --> 00:11:07.720
but a meta-analysis did find

00:11:07.720 --> 00:11:10.600
that in doses ranging
from 5 to 500 milligrams

00:11:10.600 --> 00:11:13.400
twice a day resulted
in an average 20-point drop

00:11:13.400 --> 00:11:15.120
in fasting blood sugars.

00:11:15.120 --> 00:11:16.640
There was also
a significant benefit

00:11:16.640 --> 00:11:19.200
for longer-term
blood sugar control,

00:11:19.200 --> 00:11:20.920
though this only appeared
to be the case

00:11:20.920 --> 00:11:22.800
in shorter-term studies.

00:11:22.800 --> 00:11:24.960
What is the point
of better longer-term control,

00:11:24.960 --> 00:11:26.240
if it only works in studies

00:11:26.240 --> 00:11:28.680
lasting less than three months.

00:11:28.680 --> 00:11:31.640
Diabetic foot ulcers
are the leading cause

00:11:31.640 --> 00:11:34.240
of lower-limb amputations
in diabetics.

00:11:34.240 --> 00:11:36.360
A randomized, double-blind,
placebo-controlled trial

00:11:36.360 --> 00:11:39.040
of 50 milligrams of resveratrol
twice a day

00:11:39.040 --> 00:11:42.240
showed accelerated healing
of diabetic foot ulcers

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:45.360
by about 1 centimeter
over placebo within 60 days.

00:11:45.360 --> 00:11:49.027
So, at least there's
one condition it may help.

00:11:49.360 --> 00:11:52.000
